<title>JAPAN: Japan 1996 GDP rises 3.6 pct -- EPA.</title>
<headline>Japan 1996 GDP rises 3.6 pct -- EPA.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gross domestic product (GDP), the total output of goods and services minus net income from overseas production, rose a real 3.6 percent in calendar 1996 from the previous year, the Economic Planning Agency (EPA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>This compared with a rise of a revised 1.4 percent in 1995.  </p>
<p>Percentage changes in expenditure in calendar 1996 against the previous year:</p>
<p>    (Real data)		   1996	   1995 (REVISED)</p>
<p> GDP				  +3.6	     +1.4</p>
<p> GNP				  +3.8	     +1.4</p>
<p> Domestic Demand		  +4.5	     +2.2</p>
<p>    Private			 +4.2	     +2.2</p>
<p>    Personal outlays	    +2.8	     +2.0</p>
<p>    Housing			+13.6	     -6.4</p>
<p>    Capital spending	    +6.5	     +3.9</p>
<p>    Inventory changes	  -19.2		N/A</p>
<p>   Public			   +6.0	     +1.9</p>
<p>    Government outlays	  +2.3	     +3.5</p>
<p>    Capital spending	    +9.9	     +0.7</p>
<p>    Inventory changes	  +36.2	    -60.3</p>
<p> External Demand		 -73.3	    -38.6</p>
<p>   Exports			  +2.2	     +5.4</p>
<p>   Imports			 +10.3	    +14.3</p>
<p>Percentage of contribution to overal GDP:</p>
<p> Domestic demand		  +4.4	     +2.1</p>
<p>   Private			  +3.3	     +1.8</p>
<p>   Public			   +1.1	     +0.3</p>
<p> External demand		  -0.9	     -0.8</p>
<p>   Exports goods/services     +0.3	     +0.6</p>
<p>   Imports goods/services     -1.1	     -1.4</p>
<p> GDP deflator:		    +0.0	     -0.6</p>
<p>(Note: Due to rounding, figures may not tally.)</p>
</text>
